module

public import MathFin.Models.Jumps.JumpDiffusionIncompleteness
public import MathFin.Pricing.OneDateMarket

/-!
# The jump-diffusion market at one date

The jump-diffusion model of the log return over one date `τ` as a `Market`
(`JumpDiffusion.market`): the sample space is the line of log returns `y` with the physical law
`jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw b σ Λ ν τ` as reference measure, the asset is quoted at `S e^{rt}`
before `τ` and is `S e^y` at `τ`, and the numéraire is the money market `e^{rt}`. It is the
one-date market (`Market.oneDate`) of the terminal value `S e^y`: nothing is said of the process
between `0` and `τ`.

The Esscher law, the physical law tilted by `e^{θy}` at an Esscher parameter `θ`, is a pricing
measure of this market (`JumpDiffusion.isPricingMeasure_esscher`): it is equivalent to the
physical law and compensated, `∫ eʸ = e^{rτ}`. So is the Merton measure, which keeps `σ`, `Λ`
and `ν` and moves the drift to the compensated drift (`JumpDiffusion.isPricingMeasure_merton`).
Under the Esscher pricing measure the European call is worth the Poisson mixture of
Black–Scholes prices (`JumpDiffusion.price_europeanCall_esscher`), Merton's formula for the
tilted jump characteristics.

**The market is incomplete** at one date: for `σ ≠ 0`, nontrivial jumps and a physical drift that
is not already compensated, the two pricing measures give the call different prices at some
strike, so the market has two pricing measures and `Market.price` is not unique
(`JumpDiffusion.exists_isPricingMeasure_price_call_ne`,
`JumpDiffusion.not_subsingleton_isPricingMeasure`). This is the pricing-measure form of
`exists_call_esscher_ne_merton`, which is about the two laws.

The scope is one date. The Esscher and Merton laws of the log return are pricing measures of the
market that only reads the asset at `τ`. That they are the time-`τ` marginals of equivalent
martingale measures of the jump-diffusion process, for the filtration generated by its path, is
not proved here.

## Main definitions

* `JumpDiffusion.market`: the one-date market of the jump-diffusion log return.

## Main results

* `JumpDiffusion.isPricingMeasure_esscher`: the Esscher law is a pricing measure.
* `JumpDiffusion.isPricingMeasure_merton`: the Merton measure's law is a pricing measure.
* `JumpDiffusion.price_europeanCall_esscher`: under the Esscher pricing measure the call is worth
  the Poisson mixture of Black–Scholes prices.
* `JumpDiffusion.exists_isPricingMeasure_price_call_ne`: two pricing measures price some call
  differently.
* `JumpDiffusion.not_subsingleton_isPricingMeasure`: the market has more than one pricing
  measure.

## References

* [Cont and Tankov, *Financial Modelling with Jump Processes*][ContTankov2004]
* [Gerber and Shiu, *Option pricing by Esscher transforms*][GerberShiu1994]
* [R. C. Merton, *Option pricing when underlying stock returns are discontinuous*][Merton1976]

## Tags

jump-diffusion market, Esscher pricing measure, incomplete market, non-unique pricing measure,
Merton formula, MSC 91G20, MSC 60G51, JEL G13
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace MathFin.JumpDiffusion

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Real MathFin.Contracts
open scoped NNReal ENNReal

/-- **The jump-diffusion market at one date**: the sample space is the line of log returns, with
the jump-diffusion law over `τ` as reference measure, and the asset `S e^y` at `τ`
(`Market.oneDate`). -/
noncomputable def market (b σ : ℝ) (Λ : ℝ≥0) (ν : Measure ℝ) (S r : ℝ) (τ : ℝ≥0) : Market Unit ℝ :=
  Market.oneDate (jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw b σ Λ ν τ) (X := fun y ↦ S * rexp y)
    (Real.measurable_exp.const_mul S) S r τ

variable {b σ r : ℝ} {Λ : ℝ≥0} {ν : Measure ℝ} [IsProbabilityMeasure ν] {S : ℝ} {τ : ℝ≥0}

omit [IsProbabilityMeasure ν] in
/-- **A compensated equivalent law is a pricing measure.** A probability measure `Q` on the line of
log returns, equivalent to the physical law, with `∫ eʸ dQ = e^{rτ}`, prices the market. -/
theorem isPricingMeasure_market {Q : Measure ℝ} [IsProbabilityMeasure Q]
    (hQP : Q ≪ jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw b σ Λ ν τ)
    (hPQ : jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw b σ Λ ν τ ≪ Q) (hint : Integrable rexp Q)
    (hmean : ∫ y, rexp y ∂Q = rexp (r * τ)) :
    (market b σ Λ ν S r τ).IsPricingMeasure τ Q :=
  Market.isPricingMeasure_oneDate hQP hPQ (hint.const_mul S)
    (by simp only [integral_const_mul, hmean])

/-- **The Esscher law is a pricing measure of the jump-diffusion market.** When the
moment-generating function of the jump law is finite near the Esscher parameter `θ` and at `1 + θ`,
and `κ(1 + θ) − κ(θ) = r`, the physical log-return law tilted by `e^{θy}` is equivalent to it
(Mathlib's `tilted_absolutelyContinuous` and `absolutelyContinuous_tilted`) and compensated: the
tilted law is the log-return law of the tilted characteristics (`jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw_tilted`),
whose forward is `e^{rτ}` at the Esscher condition (`compensated_tilted_iff`). -/
theorem isPricingMeasure_esscher {θ : ℝ} (hθν : θ ∈ interior (integrableExpSet id ν))
    (h1θ : Integrable (fun x ↦ rexp ((1 + θ) * x)) ν)
    (hθ : jumpDiffusionExponent b σ Λ ν (1 + θ) - jumpDiffusionExponent b σ Λ ν θ = r) :
    (market b σ Λ ν S r τ).IsPricingMeasure τ
      ((jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw b σ Λ ν τ).tilted (θ * ·)) := by
  have hθ' : Integrable (fun x ↦ rexp (θ * x)) ν := interior_subset (s := integrableExpSet id ν) hθν
  have : IsProbabilityMeasure (ν.tilted (θ * ·)) := isProbabilityMeasure_tilted hθ'
  have hE1 : Integrable rexp (ν.tilted (θ * ·)) := by
    simpa only [one_mul] using integrable_exp_mul_tilted_const_mul hθ' h1θ
  have hθL := integrable_exp_mul_jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw b σ Λ hθ' τ
  have : IsProbabilityMeasure ((jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw b σ Λ ν τ).tilted (θ * ·)) :=
    isProbabilityMeasure_tilted hθL
  refine isPricingMeasure_market (tilted_absolutelyContinuous _ _)
    (absolutelyContinuous_tilted hθL) ?_ ?_
  · rw [jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw_tilted b σ Λ hθν τ]
    exact integrable_exp_jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw _ _ _ hE1 τ
  · rw [jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw_tilted b σ Λ hθν τ,
      integral_exp_jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw _ _ _ hE1]
    congr 1
    linear_combination (τ : ℝ) * (compensated_tilted_iff b σ r Λ hθ').2 hθ

/-- **The Merton measure's law is a pricing measure of the jump-diffusion market.** For `σ ≠ 0` and
`τ > 0`, the log-return law with the compensated drift `c = r − σ²/2 − Λ(∫ eˣ dν − 1)` is
equivalent to the physical law (`jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw_absolutelyContinuous`, static Girsanov
on the Gaussian factor) and has forward `e^{rτ}`
(`integral_exp_jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw_of_compensated`). -/
theorem isPricingMeasure_merton {c : ℝ} (hσ : σ ≠ 0) (h1 : Integrable rexp ν)
    (hc : c = r - σ ^ 2 / 2 - Λ * (∫ x, rexp x ∂ν - 1)) (hτ : 0 < τ) :
    (market b σ Λ ν S r τ).IsPricingMeasure τ (jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw c σ Λ ν τ) :=
  isPricingMeasure_market (jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw_absolutelyContinuous b c hσ Λ ν hτ)
    (jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw_absolutelyContinuous c b hσ Λ ν hτ)
    (integrable_exp_jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw c σ Λ h1 τ)
    (integral_exp_jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw_of_compensated h1 hc τ)

omit [IsProbabilityMeasure ν] in
/-- The price of the European call in the jump-diffusion market under a measure `Q`:
`𝔼_Q[e^{−rτ} (S e^y − K)⁺]`. -/
theorem price_europeanCall_market (Q : Measure ℝ) (K : ℝ) :
    (market b σ Λ ν S r τ).price Q (europeanCall K τ)
      = ∫ y, rexp (-r * τ) * max (S * rexp y - K) 0 ∂Q :=
  Market.price_europeanCall_oneDate Q K

/-- **Esscher pricing of the call, in the market.** Under the Esscher pricing measure
(`isPricingMeasure_esscher`) the market's price of the European call is Merton's formula for the
tilted characteristics: the `Poisson(Λm(θ)τ)` mixture of Black–Scholes prices over jumps of law
`ν.tilted (θ * ·)` (`integral_call_tilted_eq_merton`). -/
theorem price_europeanCall_esscher {K : ℝ} (hS : 0 < S) (hK : 0 < K) (hσ : 0 < σ) {θ : ℝ}
    (hθν : θ ∈ interior (integrableExpSet id ν)) (h1θ : Integrable (fun x ↦ rexp ((1 + θ) * x)) ν)
    (hθ : jumpDiffusionExponent b σ Λ ν (1 + θ) - jumpDiffusionExponent b σ Λ ν θ = r)
    (hτ : 0 < τ) :
    (market b σ Λ ν S r τ).price ((jumpDiffusionIncrementLaw b σ Λ ν τ).tilted (θ * ·))
        (europeanCall K τ)
      = ∫ n, ∫ j, bsV K r σ (S * rexp (-((Λ * jumpMoment ν θ : ℝ≥0) * τ
          * (∫ x, rexp x ∂(ν.tilted (θ * ·)) - 1)) + ∑ i ∈ Finset.range n, j i)) τ
          ∂(Measure.infinitePi fun _ : ℕ ↦ ν.tilted (θ * ·))
          ∂(poissonMeasure (Λ * jumpMoment ν θ * τ)) := by
  rw [price_europeanCall_market]
  exact integral_call_tilted_eq_merton hS hK hσ hθν h1θ hθ hτ

/-- **Incompleteness of the jump-diffusion market at one date.** For `σ ≠ 0`, nontrivial jumps
(`Λ > 0` and `ν` not the point mass at `0`), an Esscher parameter `θ` with the exponential
moments of `exists_call_esscher_ne_merton`, and a physical drift `b` different from the compensated
drift `c`, at every date `τ > 0` the Esscher law and the Merton measure's law are two pricing
measures of the market, and for every spot `S > 0` some strike `K > 0` gives the European call
different prices under them. -/
theorem exists_isPricingMeasure_price_call_ne {c : ℝ} (hS : 0 < S) (hσ : σ ≠ 0) (hΛ : 0 < Λ)
    (hν0 : ν ≠ Measure.dirac 0) (h0 : 0 ∈ interior (integrableExpSet id ν))
    (h1 : Integrable rexp ν) {θ : ℝ} (hθν : θ ∈ interior (integrableExpSet id ν))
    (h1θ : Integrable (fun x ↦ rexp ((1 + θ) * x)) ν)
    (hθ : jumpDiffusionExponent b σ Λ ν (1 + θ) - jumpDiffusionExponent b σ Λ ν θ = r)
    (hc : c = r - σ ^ 2 / 2 - Λ * (∫ x, rexp x ∂ν - 1)) (hb : b ≠ c) (hτ : 0 < τ) :
    ∃ K, 0 < K ∧ ∃ Q Q', (market b σ Λ ν S r τ).IsPricingMeasure τ Q ∧
      (market b σ Λ ν S r τ).IsPricingMeasure τ Q' ∧
      (market b σ Λ ν S r τ).price Q (europeanCall K τ)
        ≠ (market b σ Λ ν S r τ).price Q' (europeanCall K τ) := by
  obtain ⟨-, -, K, hK, hne⟩ :=
    exists_call_esscher_ne_merton hS hσ hΛ hν0 h0 h1 hθν h1θ hθ hc hb hτ
  refine ⟨K, hK, _, _, isPricingMeasure_esscher hθν h1θ hθ,
    isPricingMeasure_merton hσ h1 hc hτ, ?_⟩
  rw [price_europeanCall_market, price_europeanCall_market]
  exact hne

/-- **The jump-diffusion market has more than one pricing measure** (same hypotheses as
`exists_isPricingMeasure_price_call_ne`): the set of its pricing measures at the date `τ` is not a
subsingleton, since two of them price a call differently. -/
theorem not_subsingleton_isPricingMeasure {c : ℝ} (hS : 0 < S) (hσ : σ ≠ 0) (hΛ : 0 < Λ)
    (hν0 : ν ≠ Measure.dirac 0) (h0 : 0 ∈ interior (integrableExpSet id ν))
    (h1 : Integrable rexp ν) {θ : ℝ} (hθν : θ ∈ interior (integrableExpSet id ν))
    (h1θ : Integrable (fun x ↦ rexp ((1 + θ) * x)) ν)
    (hθ : jumpDiffusionExponent b σ Λ ν (1 + θ) - jumpDiffusionExponent b σ Λ ν θ = r)
    (hc : c = r - σ ^ 2 / 2 - Λ * (∫ x, rexp x ∂ν - 1)) (hb : b ≠ c) (hτ : 0 < τ) :
    ¬ {Q | (market b σ Λ ν S r τ).IsPricingMeasure τ Q}.Subsingleton := by
  obtain ⟨K, -, Q, Q', hQ, hQ', hne⟩ :=
    exists_isPricingMeasure_price_call_ne hS hσ hΛ hν0 h0 h1 hθν h1θ hθ hc hb hτ
  have hQ₁ : Q ∈ {Q | (market b σ Λ ν S r τ).IsPricingMeasure τ Q} := hQ
  have hQ₂ : Q' ∈ {Q | (market b σ Λ ν S r τ).IsPricingMeasure τ Q} := hQ'
  exact fun h ↦ hne (by rw [h hQ₁ hQ₂])

end MathFin.JumpDiffusion
